---
// No founder photo in v1 — deliberately. The brief bans stock imagery, and a
// placeholder headshot would read worse than none.
---

<section class="bg-surface" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20 sm:py-24">
    <h2
      id="about-heading"
      class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-primary sm:text-4xl"
    >
      Who you're working with
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Latchpoint is founder-led. You work with me, Caleb, from the first
        conversation through to the thing running in production. The person doing
        the audit is the person writing the code, which is the main reason the
        estimates hold.
      </p>
      <p>
        The name comes from the latch: the point where two parts stop merely
        being near each other and start holding. That is the whole job. Most
        businesses I meet do not need more technology — they need the pieces they
        already paid for to catch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
